hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28022","Narrated Abdul-Malik ibn Amr, he said: narrated Zuhayr meaning Ibn Muhammad Al-Khurasani, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad meaning Ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah, from his uncle Imran ibn Talhah, from his mother Hamnah bint Jahsh, she said: I used to suffer severe heavy non-menstrual bleeding, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking his verdict and informing him, and I found him in the house of my sister Zaynab bint Jahsh. She said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a need of you. So he said: And what is it? So I said: O Messenger of Allah, I suffer heavy severe non-menstrual bleeding, so what do you think about it, it has prevented me from prayer and fasting. He said: I prescribe cotton for you, for it removes the blood. She said: It is more than that. He said: Then wrap a waist cloth. She said: I only gush forth gushing. So he said to her: I will command you with two matters, whichever of them you do, it suffices you for the other, and if you are strong enough for both, then you know best. So he said to her: This is only a kick from the kicks of Satan, so consider yourself menstruating for six or seven days in the knowledge of Allah, then wash until when you see that you are pure and you are certain and clean, then pray twenty-four nights, or twenty-three nights, and their days, and fast, for that suffices you. And likewise do every month as women menstruate and as they become pure at the time of their menstruation and purity. And if you are able to delay Zuhr and hasten Asr, then wash, then pray Zuhr and Asr together, then delay Maghrib and hasten Isha, then wash and combine the two prayers, then do so, and wash with Fajr and pray. And likewise do, and pray and fast if you are able to do that. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And this is the more pleasing of the two matters to me."
"28023","Narrated Yazid ibn Harun, he said: informed Sharik ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah, from his uncle Imran ibn Talhah, from his mother Hamnah bint Jahsh, that she suffered non-menstrual bleeding in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have suffered a severe offensive non-menstrual bleeding. So he said to her: Stuff cotton. She said: I am worse than that, I gush forth gushing. He said: Wrap a waist cloth, and consider yourself menstruating each month in the knowledge of Allah for six or seven days, then wash once and pray and fast twenty-three or twenty-four days, and delay Zuhr and bring Asr forward and wash for them once, and delay Maghrib and bring Isha forward and wash for them once. And this is the more beloved of the two matters to me."
